<title>BELGIUM: Defence ministers open meeting on NATO future.</title>
<headline>Defence ministers open meeting on NATO future.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-12-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>NATO defence ministers opened two-day meeting on Tuesday to review internal alliance reform, order a new peace force for Bosnia and try to push Russia to agree an exchange of military liasion officers.</p>
<p>Russian Defence Minister Igor Rodionov will attend the meeting on Wednesday to examine ways to make tangible progress on building a new relationship between the former enemies.</p>
</text>
